      "side": 1,
      "message": "`HighlightState` exposes a public 5-argument constructor and 5 getters while hiding package-private `interpCmd`, which still participates in `equals()` and `hashCode()` (lines 160 and 166), so states after commands like `dbg_trace` match `HighlightState.INITIAL` on every public getter yet are not equal to it and cannot round-trip through the constructor. The constructor also accepts `interpBraceDepths.size() \u003e MAX_INTERP_NESTING` (silently truncated at line 280 on non-empty lines but kept on empty lines) and allows `blockCommentDepth \u003e 0` alongside `inString`, `inGuillemet`, or `rawStringHashes \u003e\u003d 0`. Since no caller in the stack calls `new HighlightState(...)`, consider making the 5-argument constructor package-private (or removing it) and enforcing both invariants in the package-private constructor.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 58,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 99,
        "endChar": 9999
      },
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "850138e9910f8a1d106c3b2ca48c57779737fb38",
