      "side": 1,
      "message": "Opening an interpolated string shares a single unstacked `interpCmd` across frames, and lines 515 and 524 unconditionally reset `interpCmd` to `INITIAL` on `{` and `}` inside `inInterpExpr`. This breaks command interpolations such as `throwErrorAt (mkIdent s!\"foo_{i}\") \"{ \u0027\"\u0027 }\"`, `s!\"{ throwErrorAt { a :\u003d 1 } \"{ \u0027\"\u0027 }\" }\"`, and `throwErrorAt (f s!\"{ dbg_trace \"{ \u0027\"\u0027 }\" }\") \"ok\"`, causing `\"{ \u0027\"\u0027 }\"` to tokenize as a plain string and leak `inString \u003d true` onto subsequent lines (hiding `sorry`). Stack `interpCmd` alongside `interpStack` (saving and resetting on opening an interpolated string, restoring on closing `\"`) and route inner `{`/`}` through `interpCmd.onPunct(...)`, with the matching fix in `LeanLexer` (change 658563) so highlighter and hygiene stay aligned.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 456,
