      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T20:54:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When `@[...` is unclosed on a line, `LeanLexer.findMatchingBracket` discards its local `LeanLexState` when returning `-1`, dropping any open `blockCommentDepth`, `inString`, `rawStringHashes`, `inGuillemet`, or `interpBraceDepths` (for example, `@[deprecated \"use bar\\n/-\\ninstead\"]` or `@[simp /- note` corrupts continuation lines and can hide subsequent `sorry` tokens). In addition, running this shortcut when `inInterpExpr` is true lets `s!\"{ @[foo }\"` swallow `}` and `\"` to EOL and leak `interpBraceDepths \u003d [1]` across following lines. Skip the `@[` shortcut inside `inInterpExpr`, and outside `inInterpExpr` fall through to normal token scanning when `closeIdx \u003c 0` (using a per-line boolean guard so repeated unclosed `@[` cannot rescan quadratically).",
