      "writtenOn": "2026-11-23T20:54:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Calling `interpCmd.onNewline()` unconditionally at EOL (and via `HighlightState.withNewline()` on empty lines at lines 126 and 267) mutates or resets `interpCmd` while inside open multi-line block comments, guillemets, or strings, causing inputs like `trace[Meta /-\\n-/ .debug] \"{ \u0027\"\u0027 }\"`, `throwErrorAt stx/-\\n-/.lhs \"{ \u0027\"\u0027 }\"`, and `throwErrorAt «foo\\nbar».lhs \"{ \u0027\"\u0027 }\"` to parse `\"{ \u0027\"\u0027 }\"` as a plain string and leak `inString \u003d true` (diverging from `LeanLexer.stripLeanCommentsAndStrings`). Separately, `InterpCmdState.onNewline()` preserves `INTERP_EXPECT_TRACE_OPEN` whereas `onPunct(\u0027\\n\u0027)` resets it, so `def x :\u003d trace\\n[1] \"open {\"` falsely enters interpolation and leaks `inString \u003d true`. Only apply the newline transition to `interpCmd` when not inside an open comment or literal, and use `interpCmd.onPunct(\u0027\\n\u0027)` (or also reset `INTERP_EXPECT_TRACE_OPEN` in `InterpCmdState.onNewline()` in change 658563).",
