      "message": "Gating literals on `LeanLexer.hasIdentPartBefore` via `prevWasNumOrChar` breaks adjacent-token boundaries and diverges from `LeanLexer`: line 578 calls `LeanLexer.matchNumberLiteral` without bypassing `hasIdentPartBefore` (so `\u0027a\u002742` highlights `42` as `PLAIN` and `\u0027a\u00270r#\"\"\"# + sorry` fails to match both `0` and `r#\"\"\"#`, leaking `inString \u003d true`), and line 375 clears `prevWasNumOrChar` across `!` or `?` (so `1e3!\u0027\"\u0027 + sorry`, `\u0027a\u0027!\u0027\"\u0027 + sorry`, `1e3!r#\"\"\"# + sorry`, and `1e3!s!\"{ \u0027\"\u0027 }\" + sorry` walk back into `e`/`a` and leak `inString \u003d true` hiding `sorry`). Because the identifier loop at lines 590 to 608 already consumes complete identifiers atomically, index `i` can never sit mid-identifier when matching literals. Expose package-private `checkIdentBefore \u003d false` helpers on `LeanLexer` (in change 658563) for `matchRawStringOpenAt`, `matchCharLiteralAt`, and `matchNumberLiteralAt`, match `LEAN_INTERP_STRING_PREFIXES` in the identifier branch like `LeanLexer`, and drop `prevWasNumOrChar`, `matchRawStringAt`, and the 8-char `substring` slice in `matchCharLiteralAt`.",
